b0F was typical for November 13.","t_yest":"November 13: a typical high, but a warm night","p_yest":"The high of <strong>50\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 57\u00b0F, and the record is 75\u00b0F (1964). The low of <strong>41\u00b0F</strong> was the 11th warmest November 13 low (tied) of 64 since 1963.","t_rec":"Washington (Dulles) has nearly stopped setting record lows","p_rec":"If Washington (Dulles)'s climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Washington (Dulles) has set <strong class=\"sig\">43 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 151 that chance alone would give, and <strong>175 record highs</strong>, close to the 151 that chance alone would give. The 1990s hold the most record highs of any decade (70). Washington (Dulles)'s all-time high is 105\u00b0F, on July 22, 2011.","t_chg":"Washington (Dulles)'s days and nights both warmed. Nights warmed faster.","p_chg":"Across 63 complete years: Washington (Dulles)'s average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.89\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.74 to +1.03), about +5.5\u00b0F since 1963. Washington (Dulles)'s average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.49\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.30 to +0.67), about +3.0\u00b0F since 1963.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 11 of 12 months. Highs rose in 8 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Washington (Dulles)'s yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.25 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 43.2 inches a year. The wettest year was 2018 (66.74 in); the driest, 2007 (27.02 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 17 daily record highs, 1 daily record low"}}